WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.780
Learning multiple languages at the same
time is not something I would recommend

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:09.179
to the average Joe, but the reality is
that I'm doing just that, I started

00:00:09.179 --> 00:00:13.769
learning three languages at the same
time. Hi, my name is Luca from Luca lampariello.com

00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:18.000
and today you're going to see how you
can learn one, two, three, four or more

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:26.099
languages every single day. So the
languages I'm learning right now and

00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:32.369
every single day are: Danish, Greek, and
Hungarian. There's a specific reason why

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.989
I've listed these languages in this
order. In fact, every single day I always

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:42.570
start by learning the language in which
I have the lowest level. In this case

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:47.730
Danish. I just started learning Danish
some three weeks ago, and I consider

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:52.020
myself a beginner. On the other hand, I've
been learning Greek for two years and

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:57.840
Hungarian for almost three and I have
reached a more or less a lower and upper

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.570
intermediate level in these languages, which
means that it takes much less effort for

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:08.520
me to learn Greek, or Hungarian for that
matter than it does Danish and that's

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.140
the reason why I do Danish first.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.670
Establishing priorities is a crucial
factor in learning multiple languages at

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:32.920
the same time, because as I said before: time. It's not just a matter of time, we

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.940
tend to use this word, to throw this word
around, but the truth is there's two

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:43.330
factors which are just as important as
time and which are energy and your

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:48.700
concentration. And they're all entangled.
The reason why I always wake up early in

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.470
the morning to learn languages is
because I know that my energy is at its

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:58.960
top in the morning and at its lowest in
the evening so that's the reason why my

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.890
rule number one for learning multiple
languages at the same time is actually

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:08.259
wake up early and hit the books in the
language at its lowest level, which is

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:13.420
Danish in this case. Those who've been
following me for quite some time

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:18.850
know that I love ASSIMIL, which is a
small book, a perfect learning resource

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:24.450
for beginners and I'm using that and I'm
applying my bi-directional translation

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:29.950
technique to it, which requires energy
and most of all, requires a lot of

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:34.680
concentration, for at least 30 to 40
minutes.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.250
So after spending 30 to 40 minutes
learning Danish, I can do a number of

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:46.620
things: I normally organize things so
that I can do Greek after doing Danish

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.000
so that I can actually kill "two birds
with one stone" - actually there's a lot of

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:56.250
birds that you can hear here because
we're shooting outside - and the reason

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:03.060
why I as I said I do Greek is because I
know it's less than I do Hungarian, but

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:08.340
the good thing is that I can relax a
little bit more because I'm not using a

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:13.409
ASSIMIL anymore. I still do listen and
read at the same time but sometimes for

00:03:13.409 --> 00:03:19.590
example I talk to my ITALKI teachers so
it's a different thing I started really

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:24.090
enjoying the language that's the reason
why this comes second is because I know

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:30.209
that I have to do it but I also want to
do it because it started being fun so on

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:35.069
a normal day I set things up so that I
can start working around 9:00 and I

00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:40.319
dedicate time to learning Danish and
then Greek (before work) but sometimes,  like today for

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:45.060
example which is filming day, some days
are more intense than others, so when I

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:50.849
have really intensive days I try to make
sure that at least I take care of the

00:03:50.849 --> 00:03:54.780
"last born" of the family maybe the other
one's a little bit like grown-ups and

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:59.449
they think can take care of themselves
so to speak. So don't beat yourself up

00:03:59.449 --> 00:04:03.480
when it comes to learning multiple
languages at the same time, if you can't

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:08.340
learn three languages every single day,
that's not the end of the world as long

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:12.989
as you keep learning them on a weekly basis, 
and the first one - the "newborn" - you

00:04:12.989 --> 00:04:18.600
should take particular attention to.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:24.640
So Danish and Greek possibly in the
morning, what about Hungarian? Well, I've

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:28.720
tried to do Hungarian after doing Danish
and after learning Greek but I've just

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:32.920
realized that after that, I'm not I'm not
able to work because it's a lot of

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:37.570
intense work on languages first thing in
the morning and, you know, life gets in

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:42.910
the way, I also have to work, give lessons
teach, coaching, writing articles so I

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:48.190
told myself okay so two languages in the
morning when I'm fresh, and possibly one

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:53.560
language in the evening. I take language
courses language lessons with two

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:59.800
Hungarian teachers and I try to talk to
them around 1:00 PM and I rehearse and I

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:05.440
listen to these lessons after after
taking these lessons maybe 48 hours

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:11.110
later, possibly at night. So I just
distinguished the Danish &amp; Greek routine

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:16.510
in the morning and then Hungarian in the
evening. On top of that, I'm also using a

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:22.210
magazine which is called MAGYARUL TANULOK and the reason why my routine

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:26.500
with Hungarian is even more relaxed is
because again I have I think I have an

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:30.880
upper intermediate level so I can be
even more relaxed and it's what I

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:35.950
normally do to keep my Hungarian going
and motivate myself is to you know get

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:40.330
get to go to Hungary on and off I'm
going to Hungary in a little bit so

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:44.600
that's more or less how I organize every
single day.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:51.900
One thing that I've been doing for years
and it really works wonders

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:56.280
is to keep a logbook. I open the Google
Doc and at the end of each learning

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:01.500
session, I make sure that I go to the log
book and I write exactly the date what I

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:05.660
did and how long it took me.

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:13.980
Now for this specific project I have
created a logbook which includes all

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:18.960
three languages so every single day, at
the end of the day, I just copy each

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:24.390
entry and I transfer them into the
general logbook so that I can get a

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:29.000
clear picture of what I'm doing every
single day for these three languages.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:37.500
So the trick here is that if every day, at
the end of a learning session, you put

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.940
your entry, and then you transfer all
these entries into the big logbook, you

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:45.870
will see the progress that you're making
not in one, not in two, but in THREE

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:50.640
languages, and that's an amazing feeling,
just as the feeling that a climber has

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:56.580
when you know halfway he looks back and
sees the path that he's covered that's

00:06:56.580 --> 00:07:00.270
amazing that's amazing for your
motivation because you always have to

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:04.620
remember - and I can't stress this enough -
that language learning is a marathon and

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:08.940
learning three languages at the same
time it's like you know running three

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:12.840
marathons at the same time. You better
keep track of where are you going and

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:20.940
how much track you've covered. So to wrap
up: 1. First, it is really important to

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:24.990
establish priorities I don't recommend
normally to learn three languages at the

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:28.740
same time but if these three languages
two or three languages are at different

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:33.390
levels, that's fine. 2. Point number two is
that it's really important not only to

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:38.700
organize your time but to organize your
energy and your concentration. 3 And third

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:44.490
make sure that you keep accurate track
of your progress, do keep one single logbook

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:48.420
for each language but also make sure
that you have a bigger logbook where you

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:52.890
can see the entire framework and the
entire picture that you are drawing for

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:56.730
your future. So, if you've enjoyed the
video, please share it around if you

00:07:56.730 --> 00:08:00.720
haven't subscribed, please subscribe and
click on the link below because there's

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:04.830
an amazing article waiting for you with
a big surprise: for the first time I've

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:09.330
decided to publish my Google Doc where
I'm writing each and every single day

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:13.350
what I do with these three languages so
you can see every single day you have

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:18.030
free access to what I do with comments
and tips, and considerations and

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:23.180
observations that are right there every
single day. Enjoy!

00:08:31.129 --> 00:08:35.029
you

